    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner: **true when any of** the owner is a possible duplicate, the email domain is disposable-adjacent, or the city is over its soft capacity; otherwise false. It's derived on read, so it appears on both the `POST /api/owners` create response and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (documenting the three triggering conditions). The generator produces `riskFlag` on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`model/EmailDomains.java`** (new) \u2014 single source of truth for the disposable blocklist (`DISPOSABLE`) plus `isDisposableAdjacent(email)`. A domain is disposable-adjacent when it isn't itself blocklisted but sits next to one: a subdomain of a blocked domain (e.g. `inbox.mailinator.com`) or a domain sharing a blocked second-level label under a different suffix (e.g. `mailinator.net`, `tempmail.io`). Placed in `model` beside `OwnerIdentity`/`CityRegions` to avoid a package cycle.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `toRiskFlag(owner)` expression mapping that ORs `possibleDuplicate`, `EmailDomains.isDisposableAdjacent(email)`, and `capacityWarning` (the persisted \"city at/over soft capacity of 40\" signal).\n\n4. **`function/owner/EnsureEmailDomainAllowed.java`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `EmailDomains.DISPOSABLE`/`domainOf` so the exact-reject blocklist and the adjacency check can't drift apart. Behaviour unchanged: exact disposable domains still 400; near-variants pass and instead surface via `riskFlag`.\n\nThe single existing/new acceptance test (`riskFlag` false for a normal structured owner, which has no email) passes, along with a full `mvn test` (BUILD SUCCESS).",
